WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.249
Possessives and Plurals

00:00:02.629 --> 00:00:05.983
Apostrophes show ownership. Never plurals.

00:00:07.183 --> 00:00:08.273
How to spot it

00:00:08.673 --> 00:00:10.785
The same word, apostrophe moved

00:00:11.335 --> 00:00:13.603
A noun followed by what it might own

00:00:14.153 --> 00:00:17.110
It’s testing: plurals versus possessives

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:19.076
The method

00:00:19.476 --> 00:00:22.295
Step 1: Does it own the next word?

00:00:22.575 --> 00:00:24.555
No? No apostrophe.

00:00:25.105 --> 00:00:27.845
Step 2: One owner or many?

00:00:28.125 --> 00:00:30.800
Look for clues like “two” or “its”.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:34.102
Step 3: Place the apostrophe

00:00:34.382 --> 00:00:38.741
One owner: ’s. Many: s’.

00:00:39.291 --> 00:00:42.176
Step 4: Pronouns never take one

00:00:42.456 --> 00:00:43.339
its, their, whose

00:00:43.889 --> 00:00:44.983
In a few words

00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:46.949
Own it? One or many?

00:00:48.149 --> 00:00:48.931
The rules

00:00:49.331 --> 00:00:50.630
Plural: just s

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:52.341
Wrong: The plant’s bloom.

00:00:52.621 --> 00:00:54.083
Right: The plants bloom.

00:00:54.633 --> 00:00:57.077
One owner: ’s

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.963
Right: the singer’s album

00:00:59.513 --> 00:01:02.101
Many owners: s’

00:01:02.381 --> 00:01:04.713
Right: the residents’ campaign

00:01:05.263 --> 00:01:08.243
Irregular plurals: ’s

00:01:08.523 --> 00:01:10.256
Wrong: the childrens’ section

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:12.342
Right: the children’s section

00:01:12.892 --> 00:01:15.287
its = possessive, it’s = it is

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:17.618
Wrong: The town and it’s festival

00:01:17.898 --> 00:01:20.080
Right: The town and its festival

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:23.032
Decades: no apostrophe

00:01:23.312 --> 00:01:25.081
Wrong: the 1950’s

00:01:25.361 --> 00:01:27.179
Right: the 1950s

00:01:28.379 --> 00:01:29.440
Let’s try one

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:35.780
In the 1960s, the ______ campaign to protect the wetland convinced the state to declare it a nature

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:36.493
reserve.

00:01:37.143 --> 00:01:39.156
Does the word own the next one?

00:01:39.156 --> 00:01:41.776
The campaign belongs to the residents.

00:01:41.776 --> 00:01:43.472
So yes, it’s possessive.

00:01:44.022 --> 00:01:48.672
One resident, or many? Residents organising a campaign: many.

00:01:49.222 --> 00:01:52.837
Many owners: s, then the apostrophe. Choice C.

00:01:54.037 --> 00:01:55.106
Common traps

00:01:55.506 --> 00:01:57.100
The plural apostrophe

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:00.129
If nothing is owned, there’s no apostrophe.

00:02:00.679 --> 00:02:02.049
it’s vs its

00:02:02.329 --> 00:02:05.287
Say “it is”. If it breaks, use its.

00:02:06.487 --> 00:02:08.136
Possessives and Plurals

00:02:08.416 --> 00:02:10.231
Own it? One or many?

00:02:10.781 --> 00:02:11.361
Spot it

00:02:11.561 --> 00:02:13.969
Same word, apostrophe moved around

00:02:14.519 --> 00:02:15.226
Steps

00:02:15.426 --> 00:02:17.323
1. Does it own the next word?

00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:19.122
2. One owner or many?

00:02:19.402 --> 00:02:23.126
3. One: ’s · Many: s’

00:02:23.406 --> 00:02:25.516
4. Pronouns never: its, their, whose

00:02:26.066 --> 00:02:26.791
Remember

00:02:26.991 --> 00:02:29.632
Plural = just s (the plants)

00:02:29.912 --> 00:02:33.761
children’s, women’s (irregular + ’s)

00:02:34.041 --> 00:02:37.203
its = belongs to it; it’s = it is

00:02:37.483 --> 00:02:40.214
1950s (no apostrophe)

00:02:40.764 --> 00:02:41.205
Trap

00:02:41.405 --> 00:02:43.557
An apostrophe on a plain plural

00:02:44.307 --> 00:02:47.725
